docker cp 4a84109aeb44:/opt/apache-jmeter-5.5/bin/examples .
entire examples folder of the container is copied under the local directory

>>docker run --rm --mount "type=bind,source=D:/jmeter-docker/jmeter-docker-results/examples,target=/tests" jmeter-docker -n -t /tests/CSVSample.jmx -l /tests/CSVSample.jtl


Note:-
 What This Does:
--rm: Automatically removes the container after it finishes.

--mount: Binds your local folder D:\jmeter-docker\jmeter-docker-results\examples to /tests inside the container.

-n: Runs JMeter in non-GUI mode.

-t /tests/CSVSample.jmx: Specifies the test plan to run (must exist in the mounted folder).

-l /tests/CSVSample.jtl: Saves the results to a .jtl file in the same folder.

